<!--Post: 8636--><!--Time: 1109259293-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8636"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While I have mixed feelings about the recent calls for legal action to release all of the BTK investigation&#39;s information - IF there are legitimate reasons for the WPD to have been withholding information all this time - it is clearly time for something to change.  <BR> <BR>After 31 years of following the same investigative plan and getting nowhere, a new approach can&#39;t hurt. How can the results possibly be any worse than what they are now? <BR>History is replete with examples of varying degrees of success with this type of action, the most obvious example being the capture of UnaBomb suspect Theodore Kazinski after he demanded the release of his entire manifesto and his own brother recognized it and turned him in.  <BR> <BR>BTK&#39;s known writings are gramatically, stylistically and most importantly psychologically unique enough for someone to recognize as belonging to a unique individual, and BTK probably has had enough memorable dealings with people under his real name that someone would recognize that real person in BTK&#39;s writings and make the connection.  <BR> <BR>The WPD cannot continue to simply bury all information under the guise of &#34;protecting the integrity of the investigation&#34; without giving a truthful report of exactly where they are, how close they feel they are in finding BTK, or at least how the investigation is progressing. They refuse to ever take any questions from the press, they refuse to release any information to the public, and they have had virtually no investigative success themselves. As time continues to go by there appear to be fewer and fewer legitimate reasons to withhold information from the public, and the public is becoming more and more convinced that the investigation has no integrity at all left to protect, which is not true and a dangerous perception for the public to share.  <BR> <BR>I have a lot of respect for Lt. Landwehr and how he has appeared to salvage the wreck of an investigation that he inherited, but he needs to realize that 31 years of failure and the mantra of &#34;trust us to investigate; after all, we are the police&#34; simply will not do any more. The public simply do not possess that trust anymore. Period. <BR> <BR>31 years of failure to capture one of the most vicious offenders in the history of serial crime is an almost impossible record for the WPD to rationalize, defend or explain. While we certainly need to keep Lt. Landwehr in charge of this investigation, we also need some basic accountability and a much greater perception that the WPD, and for that matter the KBI and the FBI, are acting with integrity and deliberate professionalism, and are honestly trying everything they can to solve this mystery and capture this animal. That includes releasing as much information as is appropriate &#40;that means everything that does not DIRECTLY AND IMMEDIATELY compromise the most fundamental aspects of the investigation&#41; and actually inviting and relying on the public to actually and meaningfully offer thier assistance. To date, those appeals for the public&#39;s help have sounded much more like a cheerleading session for the status quo than anything else - and that just simply will no longer be tolerated by an increadingly frightened and frustrated public. THAT is why this legal action to open up the files, which could backfire tragically, is being taken.  <BR> <BR>Lt. Landwher&#39;s superiors need to give him the complete freedom of action and all of the resources, in funding, manpower and forensic technology, that he requests, needs and wants. In my view, they have thrust the entire responsibility for the successful resolution of this investigation on Lt. Landwehr without giving him anywhere near the resources he needs to to do so.  <BR> <BR>So, my modest proposal at this juncture? Let Landwehr be Landwehr. If we give Lt. Landwehr not only the responsibility he already has, but also everything he needs in both terms of resources and legal authority unimpeded by politics to do so, I think that BTK will be warming a very uncomfortable seat in the Sedgewick County Dentention Center in short order. <BR> <BR>Lt. Landwehr needs to also have the conviction, courage and common sense to be Landwehr. He needs to ask the KBI, FBI and others for more meaningful assistance than simply authenticating communications that everyone is already pretty sure comes from BTK and use the full force of the resources of both Kansas and the United States to put this killer behind the key once and for all. He needs to take and answer as completely as possible any questions the press has, rather than reading highly controlled prepard statements to the press. While I understand the need to parse those prepared statements incredibly carefully, he needs to have more confidence in his ability to resond to questions and make comments about the case that will help. I and many others also have that confidence in his abilites. Continued failure may begin to unfairly erode that well deserved confidence the public has in the investigation&#39;s leader. <BR> <BR>Let Landwehr be Landwher with all the resources he needs, and BTK will be known by his real name soon enough. Let&#39;s all get behind the WPD, and let the WPD get behind us by showing us everything they have within reason. We cannot continue on like we have for the last 31 years. I am now 44 years old and I remember hearing about the Otero murders and being horrified - when I was 13. It is time to put politics and egos and arrogance and turf wars and whatever else is getting in the way aside and end this - now. No other result will do, either for the WPD or for the public.  <BR>The public have no desire for a historian to identify BTK in the far distant future - the public and WPD acting together can catch and convict this animal now!. Let&#39;s get going! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8636-->
