<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8705"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Landwehr needs to appoint one of his top people to the post of Press Liason to handle questions. <BR> <BR>Keeping track of what information should and should not be released is a full time job. Since he can&#39;t keep the investigation focused, and deal with the press at the same time effectively, he is simply ignoring the press. <BR> <BR>Dude...bring someone up to speed, schedule a 30 minute meeting, first thing every morning with all the top dogs, to update the &#34;allowable public information list&#34;, then throw the unenvyable soul to the wolves. <BR> <BR>Then go find BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
